# Bot-churned audit state files, rewritten by crons tens-to-hundreds of times
# per 3 days. Each writer emits a COMPLETE fresh snapshot (latest-wins), so they
# don't need a real 3-way merge. Without a merge driver a human's plain `git
# merge` to main conflicts on them. CI bots do NOT use these drivers: push-with-
# retry.sh resolves with `git rebase -X theirs` / `git merge -X ours` (strategy
# options, not the per-path attribute). The driver matters ONLY for a human's
# bare `git merge`. See Notion 387637c5-416f-8114.
#   union  → append-only JSONL log: keep both sides' lines, never conflicts (git built-in).
#   ours   → single-state JSON: keep on-branch side; next cron regenerates. Requires
#            `git config merge.ours.driver true` (registered by setup-local-data.sh;
#            enforced by test.yml lint-workflows "merge drivers registered" guard).
# SAFETY: only BOT-WRITTEN, never-hand-edited files belong under `ours` — because
# `ours` keeps the on-branch side and silently discards the other side's edits.
# Human-editable/served data (admin locks, tony odds, public/data/shows) must NOT
# go here; they need real 3-way merges.
data/audit/stage-latency.jsonl merge=union
# Bot-only append log, written by scripts/lib/owner-alert-router.js. 5+
# workflows call routeAlert(disposition='auto') from separate jobs, not just
# data-health-check.yml's concurrency-guarded run (card #374 /what-else
# finding) — merge=union concatenates both sides on conflict instead of
# picking one, so a race between two callers loses zero rows at the git
# level (each JSON line is independent; duplicates are harmless to read).
data/audit/alert-router-attempts.jsonl merge=union
# Bot-only append log (task #784/#752), written by scripts/lib/provider-
