# merge-coverage=exempt — a CUSTOM attribute read ONLY by audit-churn-merge-
# coverage.js to suppress false "needs a merge driver" flags; git ignores it for
# merging. These files are high-churn but INTENTIONALLY have no driver, for one
# of two reasons:
#   (a) served / human-editable → needs a real 3-way merge, must NOT be `ours`
#       (ours silently drops the other side). Same rule as the SAFETY note above.
#   (b) cross-run accumulate-state (append array / seen-set) → neither `ours`
#       (drops new entries) nor `union` (corrupts JSON) is correct; the bot
#       re-accumulates next run, so the churn is accepted rather than driven.
# Adding a real `merge=` driver to any of these later auto-clears the exemption.
public/** merge-coverage=exempt
